Package: wayparam
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: fetch and normalize parameterized URLs from the Wayback CDX API
 wayparam queries the Internet Archive Wayback Machine CDX API to retrieve
 historical URLs for a host (or a list of hosts), filters out common
 static/boring URLs, and outputs normalized URLs that contain query
 parameters.
 .
 By default query parameter values are replaced with a placeholder (FUZZ),
 which makes the output suitable for sharing and for fuzzing workflows. The
 tool does not crawl the target: it only queries the public Wayback CDX API,
 which makes it usable in passive OSINT and reconnaissance workflows.

Package: wayparam-gui
Architecture: all
Depends:
 wayparam (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: local web interface for wayparam
 wayparam collects historical URLs with query parameters from the Internet
 Archive Wayback CDX API. This package adds wayparam-gui, which serves a small
 web interface on the loopback interface and streams results to the browser as
 they are found.
 .
 The interface binds to 127.0.0.1 only, requires a per-process random token on
 every request and rejects unexpected Host headers, because it performs
 outbound requests on behalf of whoever can reach it.
 .
 Install this package only if you want the interface: the wayparam command
 itself has no use for it.
